<!-- UX NOTES PANEL -->
<button class="notes-toggle" onclick="document.getElementById('notesPanel').classList.toggle('open')">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14"><path d="M1 3 L13 3 M1 7 L10 7 M1 11 L7 11"/></svg>
  UX Notes
</button>

<div class="notes-panel" id="notesPanel">
  <div class="notes-header">
    <h2>UX Audit Notes</h2>
    <button class="notes-close" onclick="document.getElementById('notesPanel').classList.remove('open')">×</button>
  </div>
  <div class="notes-body">

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>Navigation</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">Transparent nav that darkens on scroll preserves the hero visual impact while maintaining accessibility once users move past the fold.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">Mega-menu for Charter and Sales items recommended — brief brief lists Charter Types, Fleet, Destinations as sub-items to reduce depth of navigation.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text">Use Elementor Pro or Bricks Builder + custom nav walker. WPML or Polylang for the four language variants with hreflang tags.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>Search & Filtering</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-crit">Critical</span>
        <span class="note-text">The hero search bar must use tabbed switching between Charter / Sales / Brokerage — different filter sets for each. Avoid a single global search that returns mixed results.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">Brokerage search (Rightboat API) and charter search (Nausys API) should use AJAX-loaded results to avoid full-page reloads — critical for mobile UX.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text">FacetWP or SearchWP for on-site filtering of Phuket fleet (CPT). Nausys and Rightboat results rendered via custom REST API proxy endpoints to avoid CORS issues.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>Yacht Detail Pages</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">Sticky enquiry/price bar on yacht PDPs — visible at all times on desktop (right column) and as a fixed bottom bar on mobile. Enquiry friction is the main conversion killer on yacht sites.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">GranOcean virtual tour iFrame embed (as in brief) + downloadable brochure PDF — both require a short lead-capture gate (email) before access.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-crit">Critical</span>
        <span class="note-text">Live availability calendar for Phuket fleet is essential — clients will not enquire without it. Integrate via Nausys API availability endpoint or Beds24/Lodgify if simpler.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>Multi-language</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text">WPML (recommended for WooCommerce-adjacent setups) or Polylang Pro. Russian and Chinese market audiences require separate content strategies — not just auto-translation.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">Currency switcher (€ / THB) using a lightweight plugin (e.g. Aelia Currency Switcher) — bind THB display to Phuket fleet pages only; worldwide charter stays in EUR.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>Client Portal</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-crit">Critical</span>
        <span class="note-text">Post-booking login portal is a significant build — scope carefully. Core MVP: booking summary, crew list upload form, extras selection, base info docs. Avoid scope creep in Phase 1.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text">Build as a restricted WordPress member area using Ultimate Member or WP User Manager. Custom post type per booking linked to user account. Phase 2 can add real-time extras marketplace.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>Performance & SEO</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-rec">Rec</span>
        <span class="note-text">Hero video: serve WebM/MP4 with a high-quality AVIF/WebP poster image. Lazy-load below-fold images. Destination pages are prime SEO real estate — target "yacht charter [destination]" long-tails.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text">Yoast SEO Premium or Rank Math Pro. WP Rocket for caching/performance. Cloudflare CDN mandatory for Asia-Pacific audience (Thai server latency is punishing for European/Russian users).</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note-section">
      <h3>WordPress Stack Recommendation</h3>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text"><strong>Theme:</strong> Custom child theme on GeneratePress or Bricks Builder (better performance than Elementor for image-heavy sites).</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text"><strong>Key plugins:</strong> WPML, ACF Pro (custom fields for specs), FacetWP, WP Rocket, Yoast Premium, Gravity Forms (enquiry routing), Ultimate Member (portal).</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-item">
        <span class="note-badge nb-info">WP</span>
        <span class="note-text"><strong>Hosting:</strong> Kinsta or WP Engine (both have Singapore/Asia nodes). Cloudflare in front. Estimate 50–80GB media storage for high-res yacht photography.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

